    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.completion\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIn a scenario where function arguments are wrapped on their respective lines to comply with wrap limits, placing the cursor after one of the parameter commas results in an unintended \"overlaps\" of the preceding line by the signature helper.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nv0.9.0\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Write a function that triggers signature helper.\r\n2. Wrap arguments onto their individual lines.\r\n3. Place the cursor following a comma in one of the arguments.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nIt is expected that the signature helper consistently appears above the function line, regardless of cursor position and/or parameter wrapping.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/7c9e3403-aac0-4d4b-bbd7-42f095a71f88)\r\n\r\n[Screencast from 2023-05-24 14-09-55.webm](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/3da3a667-ea1e-40bf-b2cb-4f06123dfb17)\r\n",
