            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> Thanks for suggestion!\r\n> \r\n> Do I understand you correctly: in you video example you always expect signature window to be located above the first visible line (`auto d ...` one)?\r\n\r\nCorrect! \r\n\r\n> \r\n> The main reasons for the current behavior (open above cursor line) are:\r\n> \r\n>     * It seems more ergonomic to see this information right where you are typing as you are already looking at that area.\r\n\r\nIs it? I personally find intuitive spatial associations more ergonomic in this context ;) - but I do understand the appeals. If anything, my main concern is ensuring signature helper never overlaps existing texts - for instance, if you decide to retain the line above, it should be displayed at the end, similar to LSP diagnostics. That is, when reading my code, the signature shouldn't obscure its purpose.\r\n\r\nFor example, I wouldn't have any idea what the complete function name of \"g_get_hom\" was in this context:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/666f2986-2d17-4ebe-b4d5-431506aa9c15)",
