            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> @echasnovski Thank for looking into it regardless! - If you don't mind, can you elaborate a little more should I wish to look into it on my own?\r\n\r\nSure. For reference, here is the [code which computes config of signature help floating window](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a2bafb341894044e887e209fc013bf955371f9ae/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1195-L1232). It basically opens exactly to the right of cursor either at line above (most of the time) or below (if not enough space above).\r\n\r\nThe only way I considered altering this to not cover text is to possibly shift the window to right until it is not over any character. This is both:\r\n- Difficult to do in general case because window can have multiple lines.\r\n- Not universal enough because even in successful case it might end up too much to the right that it becomes unusable.",
